    "standardized_narrative": "Gross claims outstanding decreased by approximately GBP 18.8m (a c.2.6% release relative to opening gross reserves of GBP 731.7m), driven principally by favourable runoff on prior (back) years. This favourable development was partly offset by adverse largeloss developments on selected prior claims (for example Golden Ray and MSC Flaminia) and ongoing COVID19 related IBNR/litigation exposures concentrated on 2019 and prior years.",
    "raw_causal_phrases": [
      "favourable development on the back years, contributing a saving of 6% on the loss ratio (2020 - 5%).",
      "Favourable run-off of the back years contributed 45.0% to the result (73.0% last year).",
      "COVID-19 losses have contributed 1% to the net loss ratio (2020 - 10%) and has mainly affected the Accident and Health classes.",
      "The reserves have held up well to date with approximately 50% of the reserves now paid.",
      "There was one noteworthy back year claim increase on the MSC Flaminia (2012 Year of Account).",
      "We also increased our reserves again for expected losses arising from the riots in Chile during late 2019. They now stand at $11.0m",
      "The incurred claim to Syndicate 609 is now $13.0m gross and $8.6m net (Golden Ray)."
